## File Validation (`src/file_validator.py`)

Validates actual data files in S3 after metadata is loaded.

### Checks

| Check | Error Code | Severity | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| S3 file info presence | F009/F010 | Error | Missing s3FileInfo in record |
| File not found in S3 | F001 | Error | `File "<name>" not found.` |
| Size mismatch | F003 | Error | `expected size: <X>, actual size: <Y>.` |
| MD5 mismatch | F004 | Error | `expected MD5: <X>, actual MD5: <Y>.` |
| Same name + same MD5 | F005 | Warning | Duplicate file record |
| Same name + diff MD5 | F006 | Warning | Conflict file record |
| Diff name + same MD5 | F007 | Warning | Duplicate content |
| Orphaned file | F008 | Error | File in S3 with no metadata record |
| Internal error | F011 | Error | Unhandled exception |

### Result Storage

Results stored in `qcResults` collection, referenced by `s3FileInfo.qcResultID` in data records.

---

## Cross-Submission Validation (`src/x_submission_validator.py`)

Checks for duplicate nodes across different submissions within the same **study AND data commons** scope.

| Check | Error Code | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Duplicate node | S001 | `Identical data found in other submissions.` |

Only compares submissions with status `Submitted` or `Released`.

### Result Storage

Results stored in `additionalErrors` field of each data record. Displayed in the UI's "Cross Validation Results" tab.

