## QC Results Structure

Metadata and file validation results are stored in the `qcResults` MongoDB collection:

```json
{
    "_id": "<uuid>",
    "submissionID": "<submission-uuid>",
    "dataRecordID": "<data-record-uuid>",
    "validationType": "metadata | data file",
    "batchIDs": ["<batch-uuid>"],
    "latestBatchID": "<batch-uuid>",
    "displayID": "<batch-display-id>",
    "type": "<nodeType> | data file",
    "submittedID": "<nodeID> | <fileName>",
    "uploadedDate": "<datetime>",
    "severity": "Error | Warning",
    "errors": [
        {
            "code": "M003",
            "severity": "Error",
            "title": "Missing required property",
            "offendingProperty": "study_id",
            "offendingValue": "",
            "description": "[file.tsv: line 2] Required property \"study_id\" is empty."
        }
    ],
    "warnings": [],
    "validatedDate": "<datetime>",
    "origin": "Metadata Validation Service | Data File Validation Service"
}
```

### Error Object Fields

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| `code` | Message code (M003, F001, S001, etc.) |
| `severity` | `"Error"` or `"Warning"` |
| `title` | Human-readable title from message config |
| `offendingProperty` | The property that caused the error |
| `offendingValue` | The value that caused the error |
| `description` | Full formatted error message |

